{"type":"message","id":"c65f9621","parentId":"8bb0c545","timestamp":"2026-03-20T18:40:48.439Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Ran it on the new CT scan.\n\n**Kidney Cancer Detector**\n- Kidney cancer class: **kidney_tumor**\n- Confidence: **99.998%**\n- Inference time: **3.27 s**\n\n**Image Analyzer**\n- Prediction: **kidney_tumor**\n- CAM coverage: **0.0128**\n- CAM center ratio: **0.8250**\n- CAM left-right asymmetry: **0.1000**\n- CAM top-bottom asymmetry: **1.0000**\n- CAM explanation: the model again focused on a **localized central renal region** with **asymmetric spatial distribution**, interpreted as a possible localized structural alteration.\n\n**X-AI**\n- Summary: **high likelihood of kidney cancer**\n- Confidence interpretation: **very high confidence**, but **not definitive**\n- Recommended next steps:\n  1. Further medical evaluation\n  2. Clinician review\n  3. Additional diagnostic testing if needed\n\n**Important:** this is a **preliminary pipeline output, not a diagnosis**.\n\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/b0f1c107-0576-49f4-985a-1754b3411728.jpeg\n\nOne thing stands out: this new image produced **the same top-line result and analyzer metrics** as the previous runs. That could mean the prototype is not distinguishing between these images reliably.\n\nIf you want, I can next:\n- **save this run’s request/response files too**, or\n- **compare all 3 runs side by side** in one report.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_00c50fe49c97e9130169bd94a982748191af271ff60daec77f\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":10557,"output":377,"cacheRead":27648,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":38582,"cost":{"input":0.026392500000000003,"output":0.005655,"cacheRead":0.006912,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03895950000000001}},"stopRea